   "body": "Thank you. That was interesting!\nI'd like to add a few useful macros.\nThe first one is for casting a spell on the target under your mouse cursor. The macro's conditions are such that it will only work if the target is alive and hostile. If you accidentally point it at a healer friend, the spell will simply hit your current target. Fear and banishment are great for this.\n#showtooltip Entomb\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead]Entomb\n\nThe second is for sequentially applying our spells (you can use any).\n#showtooltip \n/castsequence reset=5 Fetid Ward, Razorice, Foul Mandate, Chill of the Tomb\nAnd the third is very similar to summoning archers and the king of magic; just press it twice. Unfortunately, both spells have a global cooldown.\n#showtooltip\n/startattack\n/castsequence reset=25 Animate: Skeletal Archer, Animate: Tomb King\n/script UIErrorsFrame:Clear();\n\nThis macro has two fundamentally different versions, for summoning different pets or for summoning all the same ones, but everything is simple there - I'm sure you'll figure it out\n#showtooltip Call of the Grave\n/cast Call of the Grave\n/script UIErrorsFrame:Clear();\n/castsequence reset=5 Raise: Abomination, Raise: Crypt Fiend\nor spam the button\n#showtooltip Raise: Ghoul\n/cast Call of the Grave\n/script UIErrorsFrame:Clear();\n/cast Raise: Ghoul      \n\nand the last macro for today is for attacking pets + dismounting if you are mounted.\n#showtooltip Command: Undead\n/dismount [mounted]\n/startattack\n/petattack\n/cast Grave March\n/script UIErrorsFrame:Clear();\n/cast Command: Undead\n/script UIErrorsFrame:Clear();",
   "upvotes": 1,
